% AUTHOR: implementation-absys (an agent: Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5). One text for absys, absys-depth-first and absys-wake-back.
% PRECURSOR-SEEN: no. Not any E01-E09 program (see programs/absys/README.md, batch 1C, for what was read).
% NOTATION: 1969 (.ab1): n > 5 and n <= 5 need comparisons, which no notation has; they are reformulated with arithmetic, which only the 1969 notation has (systems/absys/README.md, Notation).
% IDIOM: a relation as name'=lambda x begin {A or B} end, primes for new local names, lists [a;b] and [h&t]: Foster and Elcock 1969 (map and item, examples/map.ab1, examples/triples.ab1);
% IDIOM: a case's head as equations on the lambda's parameters: Elcock 1990 p. 8 (app, examples/append.abs);
% IDIOM: arithmetic as an assertion usable in every direction, a = b + 1: Foster and Elcock 1969 (tutorial ch. 8; examples/alternatives.ab1); Foster 1968, pass sets (docs/decisions.md rule 23);
% IDIOM: begin ... end groups the stage's relations into one conjunction, one assertion: Foster and Elcock 1969 (docs/decisions.md, Three notations; tutorial ch. 8).
% IDIOM: gt and pos are batch 1B's reformulation of > (programs/absys/README.md, P05), unchanged.
% P09c. Unknowns s, total. One stage: gen(<k>, s) and sum3(s, total), in that order, as one conjunction.
% CONSTANTS BEGIN
gk = 1   % stage 1: gen(gk, s)
gmax = 5   % not a stage constant: the bound 5 in gen's definition (P09c Vocabulary), given with the prelude
% CONSTANTS END
% REFORMULATION (R): the problem's n > 5 and n <= 5 are primitive comparisons, which no Absys notation has (systems/absys/README.md, Notation).
% gt(a, b), a > b over the integers: a = b + d for a positive integer d.
gt'=lambda a, b
    begin a = b + d' pos(d) end
% le(a, b), a <= b over the integers: b = a + d for a non-negative integer d.
le'=lambda a, b
    begin b = a + d' nonneg(d) end
% pos(q), q a positive integer: the least relation with pos(1), and pos(e + 1) if pos(e).
pos'=lambda q
    begin {q = 1 or pos(e') q = e + 1} end
% nonneg(q), q a non-negative integer: q = 0, or pos(q).
nonneg'=lambda q
    begin {q = 0 or pos(q)} end
% gen, P09c Vocabulary, cases 1 and 2 in that order. Case 1: its head s = <>, then n > 5.
% Case 2: its head equation s = <n> ++ rest, then n <= 5, then gen(n + 1, rest), with n + 1 written as a fresh unknown (SPECIFICATION.md, Arithmetic).
gen'=lambda g, w
    begin {w = [] gt(g, gmax) or
           w = [g&rest'] le(g, gmax) g1' = g + 1 gen(g1, rest)} end
% sum3, P09c Vocabulary, its one case: its head equation, s = <p, q, r> ++ m, then p + q + r = total.
sum3'=lambda u, t
    begin u = [p';q';r'&m'] p + q + r = t end
% STAGE 1
begin gen(gk, s) sum3(s, total) end
